# AWS — Access (SSO / Profiles) (Example)

Created: 2026-02-02 05:37 UTC  
Last reviewed: 2026-02-02 05:37 UTC

This is an example access workflow; every org differs. Keep the principle: **least privilege** and explicit environment selection.

## Login (SSO)
```sh
aws sso login --profile staging
aws sso login --profile prod-readonly
```

## Confirm Caller Identity
```sh
aws sts get-caller-identity --profile prod-readonly
```

## Avoid Accidental Prod Operations
- Use a dedicated `prod-readonly` profile.
- Set `AWS_PROFILE` explicitly per command.
```sh
AWS_PROFILE=prod-readonly aws s3 ls
```

## Common Pitfalls
- Expired SSO session (re-login)
- Wrong region (set `AWS_REGION` / `AWS_DEFAULT_REGION`)
- Assuming role without MFA / missing permission boundary

